---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/components.css';
const schema = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Product", "name": "Granny Annexes", "description": "Turnkey garden annexes with kitchen and bathroom", "brand": {"@type": "Brand", "name": "Revonia"}, "offers": {"@type": "AggregateOffer", "priceCurrency": "GBP", "lowPrice": "75000", "offerCount": 1}, "manufacturer": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Luxury Modules", "url": "https://luxurymodules.co.uk", "description": "Official UK partner of Revonia. Turnkey vaulted living spaces, cellars and saunas."}};
---
<Layout title="Granny Annexes & Garden Annexes | Turnkey | Luxury Modules" description="A granny annexe with real independence: insulated, heated, with kitchen and bathroom options. Planning handled end to end. Sizes and from-pricing." schema={schema}>
<div class="pagehero">
  <p class="kicker">Use Case · Family</p>
  <h1>Granny annexes & garden guest houses</h1>
  <p>A real home, steps away. Insulated, heated, with full kitchen and bathroom options — independence for the people you love. Call it a granny pod, garden annexe or guest house — ours are vaulted, buried and built for a century, without distance, and with planning handled end to end.</p>
  <div class="price-anchor">From £45,000</div>
  <div style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn" href="/book-a-call/">Book a Scoping Call</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="#brochure" style="margin-left:8px">Download Brochure</a></div>
</div>
<div class="strip">Official UK Partner of <b>Revonia</b> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <b>1,500+</b> projects across Europe &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <b>25-year</b> structural warranty &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Planning <b>handled for you</b></div>
<div class="imgph hero"><img class="real" src="/images/modular-40-interior.jpg" alt="Warmly lit annexe living room with bedroom beyond"><span class="lbl">STAND-IN: modular-40-interior.jpg — </span></div>
<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Point</p><h2>A granny annexe that feels like home</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead">A granny annexe is not a spare room in the garden — it is someone's home, and it has to feel like one. Vaulted ceilings, real kitchens and bathrooms, underfloor heating in every room and triple glazing come as standard, because dignity lives in the details. Close enough for Sunday lunch; separate enough for a life of one's own.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="navy-band"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Big Question</p><h2>Annexe planning permission and the rules</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:26px">Sleeping accommodation makes an annexe different from a garden room in planning terms — councils look for ancillary use tied to the main house. It is the single most common annexe worry and it is exactly the part we take off your plate: applications, drawings, submissions, consent. Detail in the <a href="/planning-permission/" style="color:var(--gold2);font-weight:600">planning guide</a>.</p>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">Sizes</p><h2>Granny annexe sizes and from-prices</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:30px">Compact annexes come from the <a href="/products/small-living-spaces/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Small Living range</a> (Modular 20 and Modular A, from &pound;75,000); full one and two-bed annexes from the <a href="/products/medium-living-spaces/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Medium Living range</a> (from &pound;99,000). All turnkey, all on the <a href="/pricing/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">pricing page</a>.</p>
  <div class="grid cols2">
  <div class="imgph "><img class="real" src="/images/modular-20-small-living.jpg" alt="Modular 20 annexe layout with kitchen and bedroom"><span class="lbl">ASSET IN FOLDER → ../Modular_20_Small_Living.jpg</span></div><div class="imgph "><img class="real" src="/images/medium-living-homepage.jpg" alt="Medium living annexe exterior"><span class="lbl">ASSET IN FOLDER → ../Medium Living Homepage.jpg</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section style="background:#efe9db"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">Other Lives</p><h2>Guest house, rental or teen flat</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:26px">The same building serves as a guest house, a home for a returning graduate, or — planning permitting — a rental. Its use can change as the family does; the structure will outlast every phase.</p>
</div></section>
<section style="background:#efe9db"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">FAQ</p><h2>Your questions, answered</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <div class="faq-item"><h3>Will the council allow a granny annexe in my garden?</h3><p>Usually yes, where the annexe is ancillary to the main dwelling — occupied by family, sharing the address. We confirm your council's position before you commit, as part of scoping.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Does an annexe have its own utilities?</h3><p>Mains power, water and sewage connections are part of the turnkey package; separate metering is an option if you want it.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Can it really be lived in year-round?</h3><p>Yes. Full insulation, underfloor heating with per-room thermostats and designed ventilation make it a permanent dwelling, not a summer house.</p></div>
  <p style="margin-top:18px;font-size:14.5px">More questions? <a href="/faq/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">See the full FAQ</a>.</p>
</div></section><section class="ctaband" id="cta">
  <h2>Independence, ten steps from the kettle</h2>
  <p>Book a scoping call to talk through your family's needs — or take the brochure to the person who'll live there.</p>
  <div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="/book-a-call/">Book a Scoping Call</a><a class="btn ghost" href="#brochure">Download the Brochure</a></div>
  
  <!-- BUILD NOTE: brochure CTA = HubSpot email-only form (hidden fields: product_interest, product_range, audience_type, source_page_url). Scoping CTA -> contact.html until /book-a-call/ with calendar embed exists. -->
</section>
</Layout>
